# Engineering

Engineering problems are about signals and the systems that process them. The guides start with signals: windows, convolution, recursive filters, zero-phase filtering, frequency response and filter design. Linear systems follow: state-space models, controllability, poles and zeros, and exact simulation. Control follows: optimal feedback, estimation, classical design and model-predictive control. Circuits follow: linear networks in DC and AC. Structures follow: trusses, frames, vibration and buckling, and large displacements. Power systems follow: networks, power flow, sensitivities, dispatch, estimation and continuation. Fluid networks follow: pipe networks, pumps and valves, tanks and operation, and transport. Robots and communications come last: kinematics and dynamics of articulated robots, and modulation, noise and pulse shaping of digital links. Thermal engineering closes the list: heat networks and their transients, walls, fins and meshes, heat exchangers, moist air and fluid properties.

